 "drivingQuestion": "From where do we know that extra blemishes disqualify a priest?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "R' Yoḥanan supplies the verse.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bekhorot.43a.22",
   "daf": "43a",
   "sentenceId": 21,
   "he": "יָתֵר עֲלֵיהֶן בְּאָדָם. מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי? אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן, דְּאָמַר קְרָא: ״כֹּל אִישׁ אֲשֶׁר בּוֹ מוּם מִזֶּרַע אַהֲרֹן״, אִישׁ שֶׁשָּׁוֶה בְּזַרְעוֹ שֶׁל אַהֲרֹן.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «in addition to those» blemishes that disqualify an animal, there are other blemishes that apply «to a person» despite the fact that they are not actual defects. The Gemara asks: «From where are these matters» derived? «Rabbi Yoḥanan said:» These halakhot are derived from «that» which «the verse states: “No man among the seed of Aaron the priest who has a blemish» shall come forward to sacrifice the offerings of the Lord made by fire” (Leviticus 21:21). The verse indicates that the priest must be «a man who is equal among the seed of Aaron,» i.e., one whose appearance is similar to the other priests."
  }
 ],
